class Solution(object):
    def buildArray(self, nums):
        for i in range(len(nums)):
            nums[i]=nums[i] + (nums[nums[i]] % len(nums)) * len(nums)
        for i in range(len(nums)):
            nums[i]=nums[i]//len(nums)
        return nums

        # //helps to retain new value whereas % helps to get original value
        # basically we are doing encoding

            
            * n karne se new value ek alag numerical range mein chali jaati hai, jisse dono values distinguish ho sakti hain.
            Ek important distinction:
- Encoding ke baad original value temporarily accessible through % n hai.
- Decoding ke baad final new value // n se milti hai.
Isi wajah se hum pehle poora encoding loop chalate hain aur phir decoding loop.
